<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en-GB">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ title }}</title>

<!-- Plotly loaded once here, so each figure can be embedded with
     include_plotlyjs=False. Embedding it per-figure would multiply the
     file size by the number of charts for no benefit. -->
<script src="https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-2.35.2.min.js" charset="utf-8"></script>

<style>
    :root {
        --ink: #1a1a1a;
        --muted: #5c6470;
        --line: #e2e5ea;
        --panel: #ffffff;
        --bg: #f5f6f8;
    }

    * { box-sizing: border-box; }

    body {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 24px;
        background: var(--bg);
        color: var(--ink);
        font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto,
                     "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
        font-size: 16px;
        line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .wrap { max-width: 1600px; margin: 0 auto; }

    header { margin-bottom: 24px; }

    h1 {
        margin: 0 0 4px;
        font-size: 28px;
        font-weight: 600;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    }

    .period {
        margin: 0;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 17px;
    }

    /* Map takes the bulk of the width; side panel sits to its right and
       drops underneath on narrow screens. */
    .layout {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 3fr) minmax(280px, 1fr);
        gap: 20px;
        align-items: start;
    }

    @media (max-width: 1100px) {
        .layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    }

    .panel {
        background: var(--panel);
        border: 1px solid var(--line);
        border-radius: 8px;
        padding: 16px;
    }

    .panel h2 {
        margin: 0 0 12px;
        font-size: 15px;
        font-weight: 600;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        color: var(--muted);
    }

    .panel--map { padding: 8px; }

    .stat { margin-bottom: 14px; }

    .stat__value {
        font-size: 24px;
        font-weight: 600;
        line-height: 1.2;
    }

    .stat__label {
        font-size: 13px;
        color: var(--muted);
    }

    footer {
        margin-top: 24px;
        padding-top: 16px;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 13px;
    }

    footer ul { margin: 8px 0 0; padding-left: 18px; }
    footer li { margin-bottom: 4px; }

    footer a { color: var(--muted); }
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="wrap">

    <header>
        <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
        <p class="period">{{ comparison_period }}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="layout">

        <section class="panel panel--map">
            {{ map_html | safe }}
        </section>

        <aside>
            {% if stats %}
            <div class="panel" style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
                <h2>At a glance</h2>
                {% for stat in stats %}
                <div class="stat">
                    <div class="stat__value">{{ stat.value }}</div>
                    <div class="stat__label">{{ stat.label }}</div>
                </div>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>
            {% endif %}

            {% if pie_html %}
            <div class="panel">
                <h2>Location coverage</h2>
                {{ pie_html | safe }}
            </div>
            {% endif %}
        </aside>

    </div>

    <footer>
        <strong>About this data</strong>
        <ul>
            <li>Shows change in <em>recorded</em> crime. Recording practices
                vary between forces and over time, so a change here does not
                necessarily mean a change in offences committed.</li>
            <li>Covers <strong>England and Wales only</strong>. Northern
                Ireland is excluded because LSOAs are an England-and-Wales
                geography and Police Service of Northern Ireland records
                carry no LSOA code.</li>
            <li>Areas with fewer than {{ min_baseline }} recorded crimes in
                the comparison period are excluded, as percentage change is
                unstable at very low counts.</li>
            <li>Locations are anonymised by the publisher &mdash; each crime is
                snapped to the nearest of a fixed set of map points, so
                coordinates indicate an area, not an exact location.</li>
            <li>Source:
                <a href="https://data.police.uk/data/">data.police.uk</a>.
                Generated {{ generated_at }}.</li>
        </ul>
    </footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
